name lgb-designate-1
timeout 160

# A GUIDED BOMB BINDS ITS SHOOTER. doc/air-to-ground.md §3.2.
#
# An LGB is a SEMI-ACTIVE weapon whose illuminator is the shooter — not an analogy but the same
# mechanism the R-27R already runs, at a different wavelength: the designation travels the SAME
# published channel the midcourse uplink does (FBUnitSignature, read by the round's own comms slot),
# and the round has no idea where the point is except that somebody is holding it.
#
# The viper releases at 5.6 km from 4 000 m, CCRP, against a briefed steerpoint. The ballistic error at
# release is over a kilometre; the kit flies it down to a MEASURED 14.45 m — OUTSIDE the documented
# Paveway II CEP band of 6-9 m [T4], which is the number this file is checked against and which is NOT
# a setting: the miss is whatever the pursuit law produces.
#
# THIS FILE IS RED AND STAYS RED, and what it now measures is a DELIVERY, not a broken law.
# The 3.9 m it once reported was a 30.45 m spot-elevation error cancelling a guidance shortfall; both
# are gone. The shortfall was mostly one line: a test on the TOTAL misalignment sat over the two relay
# channels and vetoed both whenever the raw angle dipped inside the same 1.5 deg dead band the channels
# test their LED signals against. It dropped the relay out of its limit cycle about once per airframe
# short period (measured on a constant-canard step: zeta 0.14, period 5 s), so the bang-bang rang the
# airframe instead of riding above it. Per channel: 52.78 -> 14.45 m, no constant touched.
#
# WHAT REMAINS IS THIS FILE'S OWN DELIVERY, and it is sourced three ways. A Paveway II is released
# BALLISTIC and lased LATE: 8-12 s before impact [T2 ED], "12 sec before impact (to minimize the
# movements of the bang-bang control, and consequently the bomb falling short or long)" [T2 BMS TO
# 1F-16CMAM-34-1-1 4.2.8], "most users release Paveway I and II weapons in a ballistic trajectory,
# activating the laser designator only late in the weapon's flight" [T4]. This file lases 33.8 s.
# MEASURED on this exact geometry, moving ONLY the lase start (set brief_lase_s 0.1 <t>):
#     33.8 s of lasing -> aimErrM  14.40 m      (what this file flies)
#     24.7 s           -> aimErrM  12.89 m
#     13.3 s           -> aimErrM   9.52 m      the sourced window, and the band is met
#      8.9 s           -> aimErrM 196.4  m      saturated: fin on the +1 stop 89 of 90 guided ticks
# Do not relax the bound and do not move the geometry. What is missing is a lase DOCTRINE, and it is
# booked as doc/air-to-ground.md `N11` rather than smuggled in here.
#
# THE LAW IS NOT PROPORTIONAL NAVIGATION and must not be: the CCG's canards are bang-bang, so the round
# aligns its velocity vector with the instantaneous line of sight and trails the fins when aligned. It
# therefore CHASES the spot and pays for the chase in energy, at a measured ~2.6 g of authority against
# a missile's 25 g command ceiling (doc/air-to-ground.md §Knowledge 4). The wobble that costs is the
# WEAPON: [T4] "a noticeable wobble ... relatively little effect on accuracy, but expends energy
# quickly, limiting effective range" — measured here at 3.9 m against a smooth controller.
#
# THE SHOOTER IS HELD ON THE RUN-IN by its own SMS: while `FBStoresBlock::Designating` is true the pilot
# does not start the egress turn. That is one instrument read and no new phase.
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log      `missile SEEKER_ACTIVE ... mode="semi-active laser"`, NO `missile
#                   ILLUMINATION_LOST` anywhere, and `stores DELIVERY ... aimErrM` — today 14.45 m
#   UNIT_RESULT     bunker DESTROYED (a soft target dies well outside the band; the CEP claim is what fails)
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 is not the measurement. The MEASUREMENT is `aimErrM` on the `stores DELIVERY`
# line against the published 6-9 m band, and `UNIT_RESULT unit=bunker result=DESTROYED`. The band is
# NOT met and the file is honest about it. Read as the first of three: lgb-lase-broken.fbm and
# lgb-lase-restored.fbm move ONE line each.

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.90000 6.98000 4000 90.0 250
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set store 3 gbu12
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task route
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set brief_release_s 3
  wp 46.90000 7.05000 4000 250
  wp 46.90000 7.30000 4000 250
  objective survive

unit bunker
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 46.90000 7.05000 ground 90.0 0
